.TH CCOL_CREATE_CTHREAD_POOL 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_create_cthread_pool \- create a thread pool with default memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ctpool ccol_create_cthread_pool(size_t num_threads,
                           size_t queue_capacity,
                           char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Convenience wrapper around ccol_create_cthread_pool_mp with mprocs = NULL.
Uses standard malloc/free for all pool-internal allocations.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
num_threads    Number of worker threads (must be >= 1)
queue_capacity 0 or ccol_invalid_size for unbounded; N > 0 for bounded
err_str        Optional: receives a static error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a new ctpool handle on success, or CTPOOL_INVALID on failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_create_cthread_pool_mp (3),
.BR ctpool_construct (3)
